Understand how gases are produced, purified and delivered, and how gas removal maintains useful pressure and surface conditions. Begin with familiar applications and shared quantities, then follow the mechanisms into engineering evidence.

**Begin:** [Read gas and vacuum systems from everyday use to research](foundations/Read-gas-and-vacuum-systems-from-everyday-use-to-research.lingua#r_0M6W85ATXCSSQAQBVYK0PZYTAQ).

The opening covers pressure, amount, composition, purity, flow and point-of-use requirements. Production follows air separation, compression, cooling, liquefaction, coupled products, hydrogen, helium, carbon dioxide and specialty gases. Adsorption and membranes develop equilibrium, transport, regeneration, cyclic operation and trace purification. Molecular transport connects wall interactions, conductance, pumping balance, transients and differential pumping. Pump mechanisms then lead through supporting equipment into gas/surface inventories, diffusion, permeation, joints, cleaning, thermal history and measured release.

Work through the complete books and courses with the explanations, derivations and investigations. [Compare three routes to an accepted air-gas service](studies/Compare-three-routes-to-an-accepted-air-gas-service.lingua#r_4ZE261Y4XK4JFSF4W7HRFPPWGP), [Reconstruct and criticize a cyclic adsorption model](studies/Reconstruct-and-criticize-a-cyclic-adsorption-model.lingua#r_1MW00MYZAWAZS52263CS10BRAP) and [Defend purification and point-of-use quality](studies/Defend-purification-and-point-of-use-quality.lingua#r_5BF2KBEHHJXNRREY8X3322A69W) compare production and quality accounts; [Defend a vacuum transport account](studies/Defend-a-vacuum-transport-account.lingua#r_7M3TZYFEPWVTK808QB3MDMF7CN) brings the molecular and apparatus descriptions together.

Continue through [Follow a molecule through the pumping system](pumps/Follow-a-molecule-through-the-pumping-system.lingua#r_75DSZV30D0R7Q28C9ZC6BRNXRG) and [The chamber material is part of the gas system](surfaces/The-chamber-material-is-part-of-the-gas-system.lingua#r_72F06KBVTA7W551PG3G2A19AGJ). [An inspectable network pumpdown and gas balance](computation/An-inspectable-network-pumpdown-and-gas-balance.lingua#r_0VC5EBA7F2PQHGCGYYJPKGM49D) supports three further investigations of complete pumping, competing gas sources and manufactured surface function. [Review pumping, material history and the measured state](studies/Review-pumping-material-history-and-the-measured-state.lingua#r_5QS86VWMREAY4AADFCSZEB5XKQ) brings their evidence together.

Continue into [Connect stored gas with a delivered service](storage/Connect-stored-gas-with-a-delivered-service.lingua#r_72SSPTZKFHB4DTXR1MSW0KNN8S): real-gas and multiphase inventory, filling/withdrawal energy, cryogenic heat paths and storage, transfer, vaporisation, regulation, compressible delivery, purge and surface memory. Demand buffers, reserve, quality and recovery lead into three investigations of thermal storage, pressure/flow continuity and impurity removal, then [Review delivery from stored state to accepted use](studies/Review-delivery-from-stored-state-to-accepted-use.lingua#r_5YDSGAWT2X43S7P3JQ7HPBNCA8).

Continue with [From an indication to a defined gas measurement](measurement/From-an-indication-to-a-defined-gas-measurement.lingua#r_4NFJD99T219WZK4XG65H258WHR): pressure states and gauge mechanisms, realization and comparison, quantitative gas analysis, leak detection, flow standards, humidity and reference mixtures. Calibration, sampling and uncertainty connect ordinary measurements to [Cold atoms connect collision rates to gas density](measurement/Cold-atoms-connect-collision-rates-to-gas-density.lingua#r_402V0CS0ZRT79P98VSFZ6JVR1V) and a probability model of collision history. Three further investigations lead into [Review what the measurements establish about the service](studies/Review-what-the-measurements-establish-about-the-service.lingua#r_00STQ667X1Y8PNYK73F7YC4AXE).

Continue through [From accepted measurements to continuing service](operation/From-accepted-measurements-to-continuing-service.lingua#r_630TTG5JX7D6S369PE5YCYA8FX): operating states, failure mechanisms, atmospheric and thermal consequences, reliability, commissioning, condition evidence, isolation, repair and handover. Energy and helium recovery lead into three continuing-service investigations. [Define an integrated gas and vacuum system study](research/Define-an-integrated-gas-and-vacuum-system-study.lingua#r_688Z4AZXX4VM5E2000V86HCXMS) then branches into clean-process, cryogenic-helium and compressed-air studies. Nineteen advanced investigations support [Frame a research question with a testable contribution](research/Frame-a-research-question-with-a-testable-contribution.lingua#r_1948KS99V8C25NG0WYBJHGC5AR), reproduction, experimental design, model criticism and [Publish a defensible gas-system investigation](research/Publish-a-defensible-gas-system-investigation.lingua#r_1HJHMM5T1VJWZQXR7Q5VP1HCS2). [Completion and continuing gas and vacuum studies](research/Completion-and-continuing-gas-and-vacuum-studies.lingua#r_5MX0J1H6E94CJMEY6NMSNT6R44) connects the resulting understanding to further work.

**Sources:** [Gas and vacuum sources — books, methods and primary evidence](Sources.lingua#r_0KQ1MK1BQV5KMNS3DVQT2N1VXB).

Continue through [Utilities](../Utilities.lingua#r_23Z5YYXGRA1JDFD4BAM955JMNX) and [Hephaestus](../../Hephaestus.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001). Related chemical, thermal and fluid Records retain their own routes; these learning assertions select only the steps used here.

